# Everything below is OPTIONAL. With none of it set, the app works: DJ sets
# resolve from Mixcloud and the Internet Archive (both keyless), and results are
# cached at Vercel's edge.

# ── Persistence ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neon Postgres connection string (pooled endpoint).
# Caches resolved artist links durably and is what makes hand-corrected DJ links
# possible. Apply migrations/*.sql in order before first use. See DATABASE.md.
DATABASE_URL=

# ── Set sources ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SoundCloud is the *preferred* source for sets, and the only provider here that
# needs credentials. There are two kinds and they are not interchangeable:
#
#   1. Developer portal credentials — a client id AND secret. Set both. These
#      work against api.soundcloud.com via an OAuth token, which the app mints
#      and caches for you. A bare client id is rejected there.
#   2. A lone client id, the sort their own web player uses. Set only the id and
#      the app talks to api-v2.soundcloud.com instead.
#
# Setting the id alone when you actually have a portal client id/secret pair is
# the likely mistake: every request 401s and SoundCloud looks like it simply has
# no sets. GET /api/artist reports which mode is live in its `soundcloud` field.
#
# Without either, SoundCloud degrades to a search link and Mixcloud + Internet
# Archive fill the list.
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID=
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# YouTube Data API v3 key. Adds long-form video sets as a further fallback.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# ── Profiles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Discogs personal access token. Their search endpoint requires auth, so without
# this the Discogs link is a search URL rather than the artist's exact page.
# With it, the artist's Discogs profile text can also supply the bio.
DISCOGS_TOKEN=
